  message: "DONE in PR #2271 (dev fe331532a + manifest 197fbacb2). OWNER RULING 2026-11-19 (in session): option 1, TEARDOWN ONLY. The fold marks every block it saw run under a test's |setup or |teardown context (table fixture_phase_block, phase bits; a partial run only adds, a full run re-marks, a gone file takes its marks). A change to a block marked TEARDOWN selects every test the index records touching its file (answer FIXTURE); setup-only blocks are marked, not widened (562 of them on the folded index are analyzer code that fixtures run: widening them would add up to 15,060 tests).\nEVIDENCE. (1) Close test, this item's own fault: campaign 5's clear_registry drop-call (_LINKER_REGISTRY.clear() -> pass) asked of select_by_statement on the folded index: 278 of 278 failed tests selected (2,582 selected vs 173 before); record fast_smart_test_build_11172026/kihah/close_test_teardown.json. (2) Production-path tests: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_selection_fixture_phase.py, 7 tests with real coverage and the real fold, incl. a control (same change, no fixture mark) that leaves the victim out. Mutations kihah/muts.tsv: 7 of 7 red. (3) Cost: 9 teardown-marked blocks, all test-only cleanup (clear_registry, reset_cache_for_testing, clear_pattern_cache, ...); 0 of them changed in the last 400 first-parent commits (kihah/cost.txt). Full suite before the PR: 41,482 passed.\nNOT COVERED (stated in selection_index's docstring): a test that depends on cleanup but never touches the cleanup's file; state a fixture's SETUP installs that no teardown resets."  # 71fc
